Subject: [PATCH] feat: implement AWGHO clinical insights across check-in,
 report, and meds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Seven evidence-based improvements from the AWGHO Scientific Day (Tunis, May 2026):

INSIGHT 1 — Physical activity as clinical treatment (Dr. Ben Abid/MASCC)
- Add physical activity step to recovery phase check-in (days 15–21): None/Light/Moderate
- Add phase context banner on every check-in step (nadir/recovery/post-infusion) in Arabic+English
- Reframe all symptom talking points in prep report as shared decision prompts (co-construction)

INSIGHT 2 — Patient voice surfaced verbatim
- Add "في كلماتها | In Her Own Words" section to prep report (section 2)
- Pulls verbatim patient notes from last 14 check-ins, unedited, before AI talking points

INSIGHT 3 — HADS anxiety subscale
- Add 4-item HADS anxiety subscale to recovery phase check-in (hads_tense/worry/panic/relaxed, 0–3 each)
- Add hadsAnxietyScore/Level computed properties to CheckInRecord
- Surface HADS indicator (low/moderate/high) in prep report functional status section
- Flag elevated anxiety across consecutive recovery phases for psychosocial referral

INSIGHT 4 — Triage routing language
- Enhance nadir card on home screen with explicit "when to call" routing:
  fever → chemo nurse, breathlessness → care coordinator, chest pain → emergency
- Bilingual Arabic/English contact prompts

INSIGHT 5 — Survivorship and Tamoxifen adherence
- Add Tamoxifen streak counter to medications screen (30/90/180-day milestones)
- Progress bar to next milestone with clinical context note in Arabic+English
- Add weight_changes to monitoring phase standard symptoms

INSIGHT 6 — Functional status in prep report
- Add "الوضع الوظيفي | Functional Status" section to prep report (section 5)
- Counts interference days from existing interferenceAnswers data
- Shows physical activity distribution from recovery check-ins
- Includes HADS anxiety indicator with elevation flag

INSIGHT 7 — Arabic MSA from the start
- All new strings written in Arabic MSA from the start (bilingual display)
- Phase context lines, HADS questions, physical activity labels all bilingual

Backend: physicalActivity (String?) and hadsScores (Map<String,int>) added to
CheckInRecord and UserSession. No new tables beyond what insight summary specified.

